   The strings iOS shows before the app has drawn anything: the name under the
   icon, and the sentence in the permission dialog.

   This file existing at all is what makes the app multilingual. iOS decides an
   app's language from the .lproj folders in the app bundle - with none, it
   treats the app as English-only, and then even the catalogue inside S3mailKit
   resolves to English no matter what the phone is set to. The translations were
   there and unreachable. */

"CFBundleDisplayName" = "s3mail";
"NSCameraUsageDescription" = "The camera reads the QR code that sets this device up. It is used for nothing else.";
